Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  21 AUG 95 at 17 38 CLINICAL DATA  History of breast cancer  Sentinel lymph node mapping                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  90   REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  10   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL MARGIN   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODE  INTRAPARENCHYMAL   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 4 OF 41 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  In three left axillary lymph nodes  the metastasis measures less than 0 2cm in greatest dimension in tissue section  The tumor extends beyond the capsule of one lymph node  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL  393   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES WITH EXTENSION INTO AXILLARY FAT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 AUG 95 at 17 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Medial breast margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan gray tissue fragment  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  1  now A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tumor and block with left axillary nodes  level 1 and level 2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm specimen consisting of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm fragment of breast with attached axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm skin ellipse overlying the breast  1 5cm deep to the skin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm well circumscribed  gray white  glistening nodule with a cut gritty surface  This mass is 0 6cm closest to the nearest  inferior  margin  1 0cm closest to the  superior  margin 2 1cm closest to the  posterior  margin  There is a blue dye infiltrating through the tissue and the mass  Continuous with the tumor at the medial end is a diffusely thickened  rubbery breast parenchyma    The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unrema