ll defined  nodules  ranging up to 0 3cm in maximum dimension  The remainder of the  specimen is composed of soft yellow adipose tissue admixed with diffuse  grey white rubbery   focally firm to cystic fibrous tissue  Multiple  candidate lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tissue  ranging in size  from REMOVED_DATE to 2 3cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted  as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative mass  submitted from lateral to medial  to include skin  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant satellite nodules    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant satellite nodules    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative anterior   posterior margins  closest to mass  radial     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each cassette represents 2 lymph nodes bisected  one inked black    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node trisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact candidate lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior skin margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior skin margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral skin margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial skin margin  radial         PART   BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT       report_end  , 2.
